From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:51:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Add a setup menu

A CFR setup menu for the EDK2 payload, with the options in UEFI
variables in SMMSTORE, laid out as the one of the Haswell ThinkPads:
one form per category, each split into cards, and each option with what
it does, its default and when to change it in its help.

- General: About this ThinkCentre (model, machine type, serial numbers
  and UUID from the VPD, processor, memory, firmware), and the boot
  entries of the payload (iPXE, CSMWrap);
- Energy Saver: SpeedStep, Turbo Boost, Hyper-Threading, the PL1 and
  PL2 limits (PL2 65 W by default, as the devicetree) and their lock;
  what to do after a power loss;
- Hardware: the Intel graphics, its stolen memory and aperture;
- Security: Firmware protection and BIOS Lock, the memory cleared at
  power-on, VT-d, the state of the Management Engine (through HECI);
- Compatibility: the legacy 8254 timer, for CSMWrap.

The option names are those the SoC, the PMC, the Super I/O and the
common code read; the menu only offers what this board acts on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TnH4v9ZgSCT6oudGt6KtJL
